# Build context for the FRONTEND image (docker-compose: context "."). Keep
# secrets, host-OS build output and unrelated code out of it:
#  - node_modules / .next from Windows would overwrite the Linux ones installed
#    in the image (native binaries like @parcel/watcher then fail to load);
#  - .env* files hold live secrets and must never enter an image layer;
#  - the backend has its own image and its own build context.
node_modules
.next
out
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
backend
deploy
docs
uploads
.venv
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
SMOKE_TEST_*.md
